                    %a{:href => "#D4EndingOnNS5"} D4-branes ending on NS5-branes
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#D6BranesEndingOnNS5Branes"} D6-branes ending on NS5-branes
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#D6BranesIntersectingD8BranesOverNS5Branes"} D6 branes intersecting D8-branes over NS5-branes
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#NSHalfBranes"} NS5 half-branes
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#webs"} Webs
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#NS5D4D2BoundStates"} NS5/D4/D2 bound states
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_khovanov_homology"} Relation to Khovanov homology
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_a_black_brane_2"} As a black brane
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_a_greenschwarz_sigmamodel"} As a Green-Schwarz sigma-model
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#under_dualities"} Under dualities
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_the_m5brane"} Relation to the M5-brane
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#intersection_with_o8d8"} Intersection with O8/D8
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesNS5D4D2BoundStates"} NS5/D4/D2 bound states
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#open_dbrane_theories_on_the_ns5_2"}
                    Open D
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                    \-brane theories on the NS5
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            the
            %em NS5-brane
            is a certain extended physical objects – a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            – that appears in/is predicted by the theory.
          %p There are different incarnations of this object:
          %p
            For instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+QFT"} effective background QFT
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string
            –
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            – admits solutions to its generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+equations"} Einstein equations
            which describe higher dimensional analogs of charged
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes"} black holes
            in ordinary gravity. Among them is a 5+1-dimensional “black brane” which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetically charged
            under the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kalb-Ramond+field"} Kalb-Ramond field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            constituting this solution of type II supergravity have as quanta the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            excitations of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            that sit in what is called the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Neveu-Schwarz sector
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Neveu-Schwarz+sector"} ?
            one calls this the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong NS5-brane
          %p
            This is to distinguish it from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D5-brane
            which is instead charged under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            whose quanta come from the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Ramond-Ramond sector
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Ramond-Ramond+sector"} ?
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
          %p There are other incarnations of the NS 5-brane:
          %p
            by the general logic of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kalb-Ramond+field"} higher electromagnetism
            the (1+1)-dimensional string has under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric-magnetic+duality"} electric-magnetic duality
            a
            %em magnetic dual
            \. By dimension counting this is a 5-brane. If we think of the string this way as the structure that supports the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            that defines perturbative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %em F1-brane
            (the
            %em fundamental
            1-brane). In this sense the the corresponding magnetic dual is the
            %em F5-brane
            – the
            %em fundamental
            fivebrane.
          %p
            One can understand the NS5-“black brane” solution to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            as being the solitonic incarnation of the fundamental 5-brane in much the same way as an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            in ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            is a solitonic incarnation of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particle"} fundamental particle
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/angular+momentum"} angular momentum
          %p
            Similarly, the “black” NS5-brane is characterizes by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            charge and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/angular+momentum"} angular momentum
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_a_black_brane As a black brane
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
                1/2
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} BPS
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1-brane"} F1-brane
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            %p
              %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BraneSolutionsInSupergravity.jpg", :width => "600"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                (table from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "black+brane#BlumenhagenLustTheisen13"} Blumenhagen, Lüst &amp; Theisen 2013, Chapter 18.5
          %h3#relation_to_little_string_theory Relation to little string theory
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of an NS5-brane propagates a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+string"} little string
          %h3#DBranesEndingOnNS5Branes D-branes ending on NS5-branes
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            may end on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            NS5-branes (
            %a{:href => "#CallanHarveyStrominger91"}> Callan-Harvey-Strominger 91, sections IV.C and V.B
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Tseytlin96"} Tseytlin 96
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ArgurioEnglertHouart97"} Argurio-Englert-Houart 97
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BrodieHanany97"} Brodie-Hanany 97
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#EGKRS00"} EGKRS 00
          %p#OneWayToSeeThis
            One way to see this is to analyze the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+de+Rham+cohomology"} twisted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identity"} Bianchi identity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mn 8
                      %mo −
                      %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mn 8
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d} F_{8-p} \,=\, H_3 \wedge F_{8-(p+2)}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+densities"} flux densities
            sourced by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"}
                D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-branes
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            which is sourced by the NS5-brane – see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hanany-Witten+effect"} Hanany-Witten effect
            for this analysis.
          %p
            Another way to see this is to assume that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            work as expected, since then the B/NS5 intersections appear as “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"}> duals
            ” of the intersections of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+string"} fundamental string
            with D-branes which exist by definition of D-branes:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext F1 on D5
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↔
                            %mtext S
                        %mtd
                          %mtext D1 on NS5
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↕
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi T
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext D2 on NS5
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↕
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi T
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext D3 on NS5
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↔
                            %mtext S
                        %mtd
                          %mtext D3 on D5
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↕
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi T
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ⋮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\text{F1 on D5}
                  \&amp;\overset{\text{S}}{\leftrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\text{D1 on NS5}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \updownarrow\mathrlap{T}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\text{D2 on NS5}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \updownarrow\mathrlap{T}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\text{D3 on NS5}
                  \&amp;\overset{\text{S}}{\leftrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\text{D3 on D5}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \updownarrow\mathrlap{T}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\vdots
                  }
          %p
            This leads to what is called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+quantum+field+theory"} geometric engineering of quantum field theory
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of these branes (following
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HananyWitten97"} Hanany-Witten 1997
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Fazzi17"} Fazzi 17
          %h4#open_dbrane_theories_on_the_ns5
            Open D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \-brane theories on the NS5
          %p
            Combining the above two items, the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theories of the NS5-branes (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+string+theory"} little string theory
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            theories” (
            %a{:href => "#GopakumarMinwallaSeibergStrominger00"}> Gopakumar-Minwalla-Seiberg-Strominger 00, section 6
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Harmark00"} Harmark 00, section 4.2
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lu06"} Lu 06, section 6
          %h4#D4EndingOnNS5 D4-branes ending on NS5-branes
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Witten97"} Witten 1997
          %div{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/NS5-D4.jpg", :width => "300px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#EGKRS00"} EGKRS 00
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} M-theory lift
            is a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            branching along a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seiberg-Witten+curve"} Seiberg-Witten curve
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Seiberg-Witten+theory#ReferencesSWCurveAsM5Worldvolume"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+brane"} intersection
            locus of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            on an “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M3-brane"}> M3-brane
            ” (see there).
          %h4#D6BranesEndingOnNS5Branes D6-branes ending on NS5-branes
          %p
            Consider a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            NS5-brane with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mn 5
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi ϕ
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∼
                      %msub
                        %mi AdS
                        %mn 7
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\sim AdS_7}{\underbrace{ \mathbb{R}^{5,1} \times \mathbb{R}_{\phi} }} \times S^3
            (
            %a{:href => "#EGKRS00"}> EGKRS 00, p. 8
            ):
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BlackNS5BraneII.png"}/
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
            factor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+sphere"} unit sphere
            around the black NS5-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 5
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{5,1}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\phi}
            parameterizes the radial distance from it.
          %p
            Placing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
            at one point of the
            = succeed "-factor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#EGKRS00"} EGKRS 00, p. 20
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/NS5InD6a.png"}/
          %p
            means to take its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            to be the factor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 5
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{5,1} \times \mathbb{R}_\phi
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#EGKRS00"} EGKRS 00, p. 7
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/NS5BoundingD6.png"}/
          %p
            Placing another
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
            at the corresponding antipodal point means to have it extend also to the other side (
            %a{:href => "#EGKRS00"}> EGKRS 00, p. 5
            ):
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/NS5InD6.png"}/
          %p
            or else to have embedded the black NS5-brane into a single
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
          %p
            Special properties
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            ending on NS5-branes were highlighted in (
            %a{:href => "#BrodieHanany97"}> Brodie-Hanany 97, section 2.4
            ): the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory becomes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+fermion"} chiral
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-lift" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} 4-spherical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            (
            %a{:href => "#MFF12"}> MFF 12, section 8.3
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mn 5
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi ϕ
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∼
                      %msub
                        %mi AdS
                        %mn 7
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi ADE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{\sim AdS_7}{\underbrace{\mathbb{R}^{5,1} \times \mathbb{R}_\phi}} \times S^4/G_{ADE}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi ADE
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{ADE} \subset SU(2)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} SU(2)
            (hence in the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acting
            via the identification
