                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mn 6
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 6
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-D8-brane+intersections"} D6-D8-brane intersections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometrically engineering
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometric engineering
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+monopoles"} Yang-Mills monopoles
            in actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            (
            %a{:href => "D6-D8-brane+intersection#HLPY08"}> HLPY 08, p. 16
            ).
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/WSSBraneConfigurationEngineeringQCDII.jpg", :width => "740"}/
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/D8D6NS5.jpg", :width => "380"}/
          %p Here we are showing
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+%28particle+physics%29"} flavor
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
              %p with
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 5d Chern-Simons theory
                    on their
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                %li
                  %p
                    the corresponding
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4d+WZW+model"} 4d WZW model
                    on the boundary
              %p
                both exhibiting the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson+fields"} meson fields
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
              %p
                (see at
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model#Baryons"} WSS – Baryons
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+monopole"} Yang-Mills monopole
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
              %p
                (see at
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-D8-brane+bound+state"} D6-D8-brane bound state
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => ""} Sati-Schreiber 20
          %h4#NSHalfBranes NS5 half-branes
          %p
            By the discussion
            %a{:href => "NS5-brane#D6BranesEndingOnNS5Branes"} above
            %em
              , a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
              may end on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
              has to be the junction of two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HalfNS5.jpg", :width => "650"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a{:href => "#GKSTY02"} GKSTY 02
          %p
            If in addition the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
            sits at an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O8-plane"} O8-plane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            = succeed "-locus," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            it appears as a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/half-brane"}> half-brane
            ” with only one copy of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            ending on it:
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HalfNS5II.jpg", :width => "400"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a{:href => "#GKSTY02"} GKSTY 02
          %p
            (In
            %a{:href => "#HananyZaffaroni99"} Hanany-Zaffaroni 99
            this is interpreted in terms of the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft-Polyakov+monopole"} 't Hooft-Polyakov monopole
          %p#LiftToMTheortyOfNS5Halfbrane
            The lift to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            of this situation is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+intersection"} intersecting
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M9-brane"} M9-brane
            (see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MO5-plane"} MO5-plane
            and at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+M-theory+on+ADE-orbifolds"} heterotic M-theory on ADE-orbifolds
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/M9KK6Intersection.jpg", :width => "650"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a{:href => "#GKSTY02"} GKSTY 02
          %p
            Alternatively the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O8-plane"} O8-plane
            may
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+intersection"} intersect
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            away from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/D6D8Intersection.jpg", :width => "650"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a{:href => "#HKLY15"} HKLY 15
          %p
            In general, some of the NS5 sit away from the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O8-plane"} O8-plane
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/NS5D6O8.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a{:href => "#HananyZaffaroni98"} Hanany-Zaffaroni 98
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ApruzziFazziHalfM5.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#ApruzziFazzi17"} Apruzzi-Fazzi 17, p. 18
          %p
            The lift to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and heterotic string theory
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/half+M5-brane"} half M5-brane
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "intersecting+D-brane+model#IntersectionOfD6WithO8"} Intersection of D6s with O8s
          %h4#webs Webs
          %p
            corresponding
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+webs"} brane webs
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/WebNS5D6.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from (Kimura 16
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www2.yukawa.kyoto-u.ac.jp/~qft.web/2016/slides/kimura.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#NS5D4D2BoundStates NS5/D4/D2 bound states
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
            of NS5-branes with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D2-branes"} D2-branes
          %p
            %a{:href => "#MitraRoy00"}> Mitra-Roy 00, section 4
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MukhiSuryanarayana00"} Mukhi-Suryanarayana 00
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JiaLuRoy17"} Jia-Lu-Roy 17, p. 12, Table 1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MitraRoy01"} Mitra-Roy 01
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AlishahihaOz00"} Alishahiha-Oz 00
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/NS5-D4-D2.jpg", :width => "440"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#MukhiSuryanarayana00"} Mukhi-Suryanarayana 00
          %p
            Notice that this includes configurations with the D4-branes and D2-branes contained strictly inside the NS5:
            %a{:href => "#MitraRoy00"} Mitra-Roy 00, section 4
          %p
            Review includes
            %a{:href => "#Camino02"} Camino 02, section 4.5
          %p
            see also
            %a{:href => "#Petri18"} Petri 18
          %p
            For the lift to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            see at
            %em
              %a{:href => "M2-brane#M2M5BoundStates"} M2-M5 brane bound state
          %h3#relation_to_khovanov_homology Relation to Khovanov homology
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Khovanov+homology"} Khovanov homology
            has long been expected to appear as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            in a 4-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"}> dimension
            al
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            in higher analogy of how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jones+polynomial"} Jones polynomial
            arises as an observable in 3-dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma : K \to K'
            a cobordism between two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knots"} knots
            there is a natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Phi_\Sigma : \mathcal{K}(K) \to \mathcal{K}(K')
          %p between the Khovanov homologies associated to the two knots.
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Witten11"}> Witten11
            ) it is argued, following indications in (
            %a{:href => "#GukovSchwarzVafa"}> GukovSchwarzVafa
            ) that this 4d TQFT is related to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory of the
            %em image
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D3-branes"} D3-branes
            ending on NS5-branes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB
            after one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            and one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            operation:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mn 3
                  %mo −
                  %mi NS
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mn 3
                  %mo −
                  %mi D
                  %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mn 4
                  %mo −
                  %mi D
                  %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (D3 - NS4)
                  \\stackrel{S}{\mapsto}
                  (D3 - D5)
                  \\stackrel{T}{\mapsto}
                  (D4-D6)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Earlier indication for this had come from the observation that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+QFT"} effective background theory
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-model"} A-model
            2d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TCFT"} TCFT
            (see
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/TCFT#ActionFunctionals"} TCFT – Worldsheet and effective background theories
            for details).
          %p
            Notice that after the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            operation the
            = succeed "-system" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mn 4
                    %mo −
                    %mi D
                    %mn 6
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D4-D6)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"}> circle
            ) along which the T-duality takes place.
          %p
            Lifting that configuration to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            gives
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            (the erstwhile
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-brane"} D4-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taub-NUT+spacetime"} Taub-NUT
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times S^1
            ). The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            wrap the circle-fiber of Taub-NUT, which shrinks to zero size at the origin (the location of the erstwhile D6, which is where the D4s “end”). The low-energy theory, on a stack of M5-branes, is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-susy+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-susy QFT
