          %h2#references References
          %h3#as_a_black_brane_2 As a black brane
          %p
            The 5-brane in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            was found as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            in
          %ul
            %li#Strominger91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Strominger"}> Andrew Strominger
                ,
              %p
                %em> Heterotic solitons
                , Nucl.Phys. B343 (1990) 167-184 Nucl.Phys. B353 (1991) 565 (
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/27900"}> spire
                )
              %p
                Erratum: Nucl. Phys. B353 (1991) 565-565 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(91)90349-3"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(91)90349-3
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/27900"} spire:27900
            %li#CallanHarveyStrominger91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Curtis+Callan"}> Curtis Callan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Harvey"} Jeffrey Harvey
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Strominger"} Andrew Strominger
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Worldbrane actions for string solitons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(91)90041-U"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(91)90041-U
            %li
              %p
                Marco Cariglia,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kurt+Lechner"} Kurt Lechner
                %em NS5-branes in IIA supergravity and gravitational anomalies
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0203238"}> arXiv:hep-th/0203238
                )
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+intersection"} intersection
            laws with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            are discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Tseytlin96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arkady+Tseytlin"}> Arkady Tseytlin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em No-force condition and BPS combinations of p-branes in 11 and 10 dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9609212"} arXiv:hep-th/9609212
            %li#HananyWitten97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amihay+Hanany"}> Amihay Hanany
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Type IIB Superstrings, BPS Monopoles, And Three-Dimensional Gauge Dynamics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9611230"} arXiv:hep-th/9611230
            %li#ArgurioEnglertHouart97
              %p
                R. Argurio,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fran%C3%A7ois+Englert"} François Englert
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Intersection Rules for
                    = succeed "-Branes" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9701042"} arXiv:hep-th/9701042
            %li#Witten97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Solutions Of Four-Dimensional Field Theories Via M Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://xxx.lanl.gov/abs/hep-th/9703166"} arXiv:hep-th/9703166
            %li#BrodieHanany97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Brodie"}> John Brodie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amihay+Hanany"} Amihay Hanany
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Type IIA Superstrings, Chiral Symmetry, and N=1 4D Gauge Theory Dualities
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9704043"} arXiv:hep-th/9704043
            %li#EGKRS00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shmuel+Elitzur"}> Shmuel Elitzur
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amit+Giveon"} Amit Giveon
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kutasov"} David Kutasov
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eliezer+Rabinovici"} Eliezer Rabinovici
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gor+Sarkissian"} Gor Sarkissian
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-Branes in the Background of NS Fivebranes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0005052"} arXiv:hep-th/0005052
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2000/08/046"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2000/08/046
          %p Review includes
          %ul
            %li#Fazzi17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Fazzi"}> Marco Fazzi
              ,
              %em Higher-dimensional field theories from type II supergravity
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.04447"}> arXiv:1712.04447
              )
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-lift" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
            should be the configuration from section 8.3 of
          %ul
            %li#MFF12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+de+Medeiros"}> Paul de Medeiros
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"} José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              = succeed "," do
                %em Half-BPS M2-brane orbifolds
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.4761"} arXiv:1007.4761
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.atmp/1408561553"} Euclid
          %h3#as_a_greenschwarz_sigmamodel As a Green-Schwarz sigma-model
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functionals"} Green-Schwarz action functionals
            for the NS5-brane:
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            (see also at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+heterotic+string+theory"} dual heterotic string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kurt+Lechner"}> Kurt Lechner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mario+Tonin"} Mario Tonin
                %em Worldvolume and target space anomalies in the D=10 super–fivebrane sigma–model
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9603094"}> arXiv:hep-th/9603094
                )
            %li
              %p
                J. Mourad,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Anomalies of the
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 32
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(32)
                    five-brane and their cancellation
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9709012"} arxiv:hep-th/9709012
            %li#Lechner10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kurt+Lechner"}> Kurt Lechner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum properties of the heterotic five-brane
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1005.5719"} arxiv:1005.5719
          %p
            In
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                , Alexei Nurmagambetov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"} Dmitri Sorokin
                %em The type IIA NS5–Brane
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0003169"}> arXiv:hep-th/0003169
                )
            %li
              %p
                Daniel Persson,
                %em Fivebrane Instantons and Hypermultiplets
                (2010) (
                %a{:href => "http://string.lpthe.jussieu.fr/QKPHYS2010/Persson.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            as a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+WZW+model"} higher WZW model
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
          %h3#under_dualities Under dualities
          %p
            Discussion of the effect of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            on NS5-branes includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduardo+Eyras"}> Eduardo Eyras
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Janssen"} Bert Janssen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yolanda+Lozano"} Yolanda Lozano
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 5-branes, KK-monopoles and T-duality
                %strong 531
                (1998) 275-301 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9806169"}> arXiv:hep-th/9806169
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(98)00575-6"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(98)00575-6
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Tong"}> David Tong
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em NS5-Branes, T-Duality and Worldsheet Instantons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0204186"} arXiv:hep-th/0204186
          %p
            On its relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-critical+string"} non-critical string
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO-theory"} KO-theory
          %ul
            %li
              Iñaki Garcia-Etxebarria,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miguel+Montero"} Miguel Montero
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%81ngel+Uranga"} Ángel Uranga
              %em Heterotic NS5-branes from closed string tachyon condensation.
              Physical Review D 90.12 (2014): 126002. (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1405.0009"}> arXiv:1405.0009
              ).
          %h3#relation_to_the_m5brane Relation to the M5-brane
          %p
            Most of the following references are more on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
          %p
            The fact that the worldvolume theory of the M5-brane should support fields that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+a+2-bundle"} connections on a 2-bundle
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
            a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
          %ul
            %li#Witten07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conformal+field+theory+in+four+and+six+dimensions"} Conformal field theory in four and six dimensions
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrike+Tillmann"} Ulrike Tillmann
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topology, Geometry and Quantum Field Theory: Proceedings of the 2002 Oxford Symposium in Honour of the 60th Birthday of Graeme Segal
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0712.0157"} arXiv:0712.0157
          %p as well as sections 3 and 4 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %em Geometric Langlands From Six Dimensions
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.2720"}> arXiv:0905.2720
              )
              %p#Witten09 .
          %p A review of some aspects is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robbert+Dijkgraaf"}> Robbert Dijkgraaf
              ,
              %em The mathematics of fivebranes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/hep-th/pdf/9810/9810157v1.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Khovanov+homology"} Khovanov homology
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Witten11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fivebranes and Knots
                %strong 3
                1 (2012) 1-137 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1101.3216"}> arXiv:1101.3216
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.4171/QT/26"} doi:10.4171/QT/26
            %li#GukovSchwarzVafa
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"}> Sergei Gukov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"} Albert Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                %em Khovanov-Rozansky Homology And Topological Strings
                , Lett. Math. Phys. 74 (2005) 53-74, (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412243"}> arXiv:hep-th/0412243
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"}> Greg Moore
              ,
              %em
